BT /F1 22 Tf 64 742 Td (Marketing CV checklist) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 64 712 Td (A one-page pre-send check for marketing and analytics roles.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 64 670 Td (BEFORE YOU SEND) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 650 Td (Read the job description and highlight the three most repeated tasks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 634 Td (Match your CV summary to the role, not to every role you have ever wanted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 618 Td (Put the most relevant experience first. Recruiters scan from the top.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 602 Td (Use plain job titles and explain unusual internal titles.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 586 Td (Write about outcomes and decisions, not only responsibilities.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 570 Td (Include tools you can genuinely discuss in an interview.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 554 Td (Keep the layout simple enough to open on a phone.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 538 Td (Use a consistent date format for every role.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 522 Td (Check that your email address and phone number are current.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 506 Td (Name the file clearly: Firstname-Lastname-CV.pdf.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 490 Td (Export to PDF and open the exported file before sending.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 474 Td (Ask one person to check for typos and unclear sentences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 64 446 Td (A USEFUL BULLET FORMULA) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 426 Td (Action + context + result or learning.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 410 Td (Example: Planned a four-week content calendar for a student society,) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 394 Td (coordinated three contributors and reviewed performance weekly.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 378 Td (If you do not have a result, describe the decision and what you learned.) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 64 362 Td (Never invent a number. An honest small project is stronger than a fake one.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 64 326 Td (Placeholder resource from Social Magent. socialmagent.online) Tj ET
